# p10 negation: "this examination has no height measurement"
#
# LinkML option: none.
#
# Two OWL forms, both about examination1 in base.ttl:
#   1. Class membership in a complement, the OWL analogue of Wikidata's "no value":
#      examination1 is a member of not (has part some 'length measurement assay').
#   2. A NegativeObjectPropertyAssertion: examination1 does not have ex:heightAssay1 as a part.
#      This is much weaker: it denies one named individual and says nothing about others.
#
# NegativeDataPropertyAssertion does not fit this sentence: it denies one literal (for example,
# "valueSpec1 does not have numeric value 1.67"), which presupposes a value specification.
#
# Form 1 uses the general OBI:0003817 class, so it also denies any other length measurement in
# this examination; OBI has no narrower height assay class.
#
# A consumer with a reasoner can infer that any assertion of a length measurement assay as part
# of examination1 contradicts the record: see p10_negation_contradiction.ttl. A SPARQL consumer has
# to read the restriction structure.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/napoleon/> .
@prefix BFO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix OBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .

# Form 1
ex:examination1 a
    [ a owl:Class ;
      owl:complementOf
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
          owl:onProperty BFO:0000051 ;
          owl:someValuesFrom OBI:0003817 ] ] .

# Form 2
ex:heightAssay1 a owl:NamedIndividual .

[] a owl:NegativePropertyAssertion ;
    owl:sourceIndividual ex:examination1 ;
    owl:assertionProperty BFO:0000051 ;
    owl:targetIndividual ex:heightAssay1 .
